hy. A string `envvar` becomes a one-item list, and each variable is quoted and joined with `\", \"`. So `envvar=[\"A\", \"B\"]` now prints `(env var: 'A', 'B')` instead of the list's `repr`. I added the comment about spaces and commas that the spec asked for.\n- **`src/click/core.py`, `Option.get_help_extra`**: the auto-prefix name is used when `envvar` is falsy, not only when it is `None`. `extra[\"envvars\"]` is set only when `envvar` is truthy, and the nested `if` is merged into one condition. An empty `envvar` now behaves like `None` and no longer shows `[env var: ]`.\n- **`CHANGES.md`**: two bullets added under Unreleased after the last entry, both tagged `{pr}`3884``.\n\nI didn't touch `tests/test_options.py` or `SPEC.md`, and I didn't run the full test suite, since the spec lists only the one command.", "ttft_ms": 1606, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 15934, "uuid": "763d5da9-a363-43cb-bae1-05525e23c877", "ttft_stream_ms": 1252, "time_to_request_ms": 306, "first_content_frame_ms": 1252, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
